; typeswatch.eval - a theme open in the type editor survives a quality change
; (code-review C235). Judged by tools/EditorTest.py phase 19, which runs it
; WINDOWED: a headless run never draws, and the fault was in the drawing. The
; theme's member rows kept the level albedo textures they were built with as
; their swatches; a quality change reloads every surface texture, and the
; still-open dialog drew the freed ones.
;
; The Floors tab is brought to the front so its swatch rows draw. Quality goes
; to 2 and then to 0, so the texture resolution changes whatever settings.ini
; held (EditorTest puts settings.ini back afterwards); each `typeset dialog`
; after a change is a frame drawn with the dialog up.

logecho on
reset
typeset dialog themes marble_hall
typeset dialog tab 1
quality 2
typeset dialog
typeset dialog
typeset dialog
quality 0
typeset dialog
typeset dialog
typeset dialog
typeset dialog rows
typeset dialog off
